From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: a733: Do not remux an interrupt pin to read
 it

With irq_read_needs_mux, reading an interrupt pin muxes it back to
function 6 afterwards, but the A733 external interrupt function is 14,
and 6 is reserved on pins such as the SD card detect pin PF6. The A733
data register follows a pin in interrupt mode, so drop the flag.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the SD card-detect pin PF6
stays in its interrupt function after it is read.

Fixes: 0535bfbfa97b ("pinctrl: sunxi: add support for the Allwinner A733")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
index bc483d983bbc..0841c04278ca 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -23,7 +23,6 @@ static const u8 a733_irq_bank_muxes[SUNXI_PINCTRL_MAX_BANKS] =
 
 static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_pinctrl_data = {
 	.irq_banks = 11,
-	.irq_read_needs_mux = true,
 	.io_bias_cfg_variant = BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL,
 };
 
